.TH WORT 1 "November 2026" "wort 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wort \- offline German\(enGerman dictionary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wort
.br
.B wort
.I Wort
.br
.B wort \-e
.I word
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wort
is an offline German dictionary for the terminal. Its data comes from the
German Wiktionary and OpenThesaurus: meanings with one example each,
pronunciation (IPA), hyphenation, synonyms, antonyms and English
translations.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B wort
starts a full-screen interface: type to search, the list on the left
shows matching words and the entry of the highlighted word is shown on
the right.
.PP
With a word, it prints that word's entry and exits.
Inflected forms lead to their base form (\fIging\fP finds \fIgehen\fP).
.PP
Umlauts and \(ss can be typed as ae, oe, ue and ss: \fIhaeuser\fP finds
\fIH\(:auser\fP. Accents may be left out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-e " word"
Search an English word and print the German entries it translates to.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down
Pick a word from the list.
.TP
.B Page Up, Page Down
Scroll the entry. In the macOS Terminal use Shift+Page Up/Down.
.TP
.B F1
Show or hide the info page (data sources, licences, snapshot dates).
.TP
.B F2
Switch the search between German and English.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the last character.
.TP
.B Esc
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WORT_DATA
Directory that holds wort.idx, wort.dat and the optional wort-en.idx.
.SH FILES
The data files are looked for in this order: the
.B WORT_DATA
directory, the directory of the program itself, then
.IR PREFIX/share/wort
(default
.IR /usr/local/share/wort ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when an entry was found, 1 when not, 2 when the data files are missing.
